{"name":"Amaretto Sour","hex":"#c09856","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"amaretto sour","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["a drink made from amaretto and a sweetened mixture of lemon or lime juice"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/amaretto_sour"}],"entries":[{"title":"Amaretto sour","blocks":[{"text":"An amaretto sour is a cocktail using amaretto liqueur. It is a type of sour, a mixed drink made with a base spirit, citrus juice, and a sweetener. The drink is the most popular cocktail use for amaretto."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/VTR_amaretto_sour.jpg/330px-VTR_amaretto_sour.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amaretto_sour"},{"title":"Amaretto","blocks":[{"text":"Amaretto is a sweet Italian liqueur originating from the comune (municipality) of Saronno. Depending on the brand, it may be made from apricot kernels, bitter almonds, peach stones, or almonds, all of which are natural sources of the benzaldehyde that provides the almond-like flavour of the liqueur. It generally contains 21 to 28 percent alcohol by volume."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Amaretto_Bottles_4.JPG/330px-Amaretto_Bottles_4.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amaretto"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/VTR_amaretto_sour.jpg/500px-VTR_amaretto_sour.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/VTR_amaretto_sour.jpg/1280px-VTR_amaretto_sour.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/VTR_amaretto_sour.jpg/500px-VTR_amaretto_sour.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbn